    "result_text": "The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both of its tests pass along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` as a response-time derived field on the owner, following the codebase's existing pattern for derived-from-stored-field values (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`util/CityRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class holding the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `locality(city)` lookup that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` (including for a null city).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` and a small `locality(Owner)` default method that delegates to `CityRegion`. The mapper is used by both `RespondWithOwner` (GET) and the create response, so the field is derived consistently everywhere an owner is returned.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` DTO schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nBecause `city` is already stored on the entity, no new DB column, migration, or change to the POST pipeline was needed \u2014 the derivation lives entirely in the mapper, keeping each unit focused. Both acceptance tests (known city \u2192 `NSW`, unknown city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) and the full build pass.",
